  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday)\nIssued at 1214 AM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nLong-term forecast impacts: Warm-up Friday and Saturday. Pattern may \nturn more unsettled beginning Sunday, but confidence is low.\n\nDiscussion: The trough combo will depart to the east on Friday, \nreturning primary influence over the pattern to the mid-latitude \njet. A couple of days of zonal-to-northwest flow over the Rockies \nwill return the lee trough and begin a period of dry return flow on \nFriday and Saturday. Temperatures will rebound to their usual perch \nin 2026 (5-to-10 degrees above normal).\n\nCompared to 24 hours ago, the trough/frontal passage on Sunday looks \nto have a slightly higher probability of impacts on the 0Z guidance \nsuite. The trough has a more coherent structure on this model cycle \nwith a well-defined surface response and even hints at a nascent \nwarm sector. NBM is not putting in any precipitation probabilities \non Sunday and that seems reasonable for now, but the period bears \nwatching in case there is an uptrend in rain/postfrontal \nwind/temperature drop chances.\n\nRegardless, this system is a bit more of a clipper, so there isn't \nmuch time for cooler air to filter in. Decent chance that we return \nto the 5-to-10-above-normal level we've seen so often by Monday.\n\nMeister",
